\subsection{Greenwashing Detector (Stage 4)}

The detector was refined through four successive configurations, each evaluated on the same labelled set. At the paragraph level (v1), recall was perfect (1.000) but precision was low (0.650) because a single generic opening sentence caused entire paragraphs to be flagged regardless of their remaining content. Moving to sentence-level evaluation (v2) raised both precision and recall to 0.846 by assessing each sentence individually. A two-condition strict variant was also evaluated -- flagging a segment only when at least one sentence is vague and no sentence is specific -- but this configuration reduced precision to 0.619 due to connector sentences in multi-sentence paragraphs that superficially resemble vague language without constituting genuine hedging; the stricter rule was therefore not retained. The final configuration retains the sentence-level approach with improved evidence patterns, achieving precision 0.917, recall 0.846, F1 0.880, and AUC-ROC 0.894. Results are shown in Fig.~\ref{fig:detector} and Table~\ref{tab:gw_history}.

