\subsection{Regulatory Alignment (Stage 5)}

Alignment scoring was evaluated on 393 text segments from 100 companies, after removing boilerplate and bare reference links. The correct principle ranked first for 44.3\% of segments -- approximately four times better than the 11.1\% random baseline -- confirming that the score is meaningful. Results vary by principle: Environment reaches 66.7\% and Sustainable Products 64.3\%, both benefiting from distinctive vocabularies, while Consumer Value reaches only 12.5\% and Stakeholder Engagement 22.9\%, both of which rely on general corporate language. This pattern mirrors the per-principle classifier results from Stage~3, suggesting that vocabulary distinctiveness is the dominant driver of performance across both tasks.

\subsection{Transparency Score and Sectors (Stage 6)}

\subsubsection{Score Distribution}

The Transparency Score was computed for all 1,164 companies. Scores range from 26.88 to 75.58, with a median of 47.25 and a mean of 48.73. The corpus spans 47 statistically reliable sectors (five or more companies each) and 25 smaller or singleton sectors. All 47 reliable sectors are used in the analyses below.

